# reaper_symshadow.allow - C-library names a vendor library answers first, accepted as stock behaviour.
# Format: "<program path in the image> <symbol>" or "* <symbol>" for every program. Read by reaper_verify.sh.
# Add a line only after checking that the vendor version behaves like the C library's for the callers involved.
#
# libshared.so getifaddrs()/freeifaddrs() (stock ASUS implementation; rc, httpd, inadyn, chilli use it on stock too)
* getifaddrs
* freeifaddrs
# netatalk's libatalk.so carries its own nftw() for its own tools (/usr/bin/ad)
/usr/bin/ad nftw
